   349	>n
   350	
   351	Cold Passage
   352	
   353	This is a cold and damp corridor where a long east-west passageway turns into
   354	a southward path.
   355	
   356	>w
   357	
   358	Slide Room
   359	
   360	This is a small chamber, which appears to have been part of a coal mine. On
   361	the south wall of the chamber the letters “Granite Wall” are etched in the
   362	rock. To the east is a long passage, and there is a steep metal slide twisting
   363	dounward. To the north is a small opening.
   364	
   365	n
   366	
   367	Mine Entrance
   368	
   369	You are standing at the entrance of what might have been a coal mine. The
   370	shaft enters the west wall, and there is another exit on the south end of the
   371	room.
   372	
   373	>w
   374	
   375	Squeaky Room
   376	
   377	You are in a small room. Strange squeaky sounds may be heard coming from the
